WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:09.718
Pachinko is an epic journey

00:00:09.718 --> 00:00:12.304
of four generations
of a Korean family.

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:17.226
Through years, we watch a girl

00:00:17.226 --> 00:00:20.020
grow up from a teenager
into a woman.

00:00:22.648 --> 00:00:24.650
This is the story of Sunja.

00:00:25.442 --> 00:00:28.403
A poor Korean girl
who becomes pregnant

00:00:28.737 --> 00:00:31.448
and has to travel far from
home to start a new life

00:00:31.448 --> 00:00:32.866
in a country that
doesn’t even want her.

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:38.580
It’s about Sunja’s
soul and determination

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:40.749
and her power to survive.

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:53.011
Every country has
their own history.

00:00:53.512 --> 00:00:56.598
Sometimes it’s beautiful, but
sometimes it’s ugly.

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:11.905
One of the things that I
was so interested in was

00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:13.865
what if you could create a show

00:01:13.865 --> 00:01:16.702
where the third generation
has at least

00:01:16.702 --> 00:01:19.204
some kind of thematic dialogue
with the first generation.

00:01:20.414 --> 00:01:22.582
There’s a sacrifice of that
first generation

00:01:23.458 --> 00:01:25.836
and the burden that it becomes
on the third generation.

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:30.299
It's incredibly ambitious,
the scale of the storytelling

00:01:30.299 --> 00:01:32.009
and how many
generations we follow.

00:01:32.509 --> 00:01:35.095
When I read the script
I was blown away,

00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:39.308
by the storytelling and the
scope and the size of the story.

00:01:39.683 --> 00:01:42.227
We travel from New York to
Korea, Japan.

00:01:42.519 --> 00:01:43.854
You needed that
global lens.

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:54.614
I think every family has
a Sunja in their life.

00:01:55.032 --> 00:01:56.199
Regardless if you’re Korean,

00:01:56.199 --> 00:01:57.784
regardless if you’re from
an immigrant family.

00:01:58.243 --> 00:02:00.203
This experience of
leaving a homeland

00:02:00.203 --> 00:02:01.747
to forge a new life
somewhere else

00:02:01.747 --> 00:02:03.415
because you want a better
opportunity for your children.

00:02:04.875 --> 00:02:09.963
We are the result of the trials
and tribulations and experiences

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:12.674
and decisions made by those who
came before us.

00:02:24.436 --> 00:02:25.479
Kanpai!

